## What This Repository Is

This is **NVIDIA'"'"'s Deep Learning Accelerator (NVDLA)**, an open-source hardware
design for deep learning inference. NVDLA implements a full-chip deep learning
accelerator supporting convolution, pooling, normalization, and activation
operations with 2048 × INT8 MACs (or 1024 × FP16/INT16 MACs).

## What Has Been Stripped

All implementation Verilog files in `vmod/nvdla/` have been **zeroed out**.
The file names and directory structure remain intact, but every module body
has been removed. You must restore the implementation.

**Kept intact:** `vmod/vlibs/`, `vmod/rams/`, `vmod/include/`, `verif/`,
`tools/`, `cmod/`.

## Test Infrastructure

Tests use a **Verilator trace-player**: each test trace (`input.txn`) is
converted to binary format and replayed through the `VNV_nvdla` Verilator
simulation binary. Tests pass when `VNV_nvdla` prints `*** PASS`.

## Scored Tests — E2E Only (7 total)

These tests execute real neural network inference and check output feature
maps against golden data. They require the **entire NVDLA pipeline** to be
functionally correct:

| Test name | Network operation |
|-----------|------------------|
| `sanity3` | Multi-layer sequence with data checking |
| `sanity3_cvsram` | Same test using on-chip CVSRAM |
| `conv_8x8_fc_int16` | 8×8 fully-connected conv, INT16 weights, data checked |
| `googlenet_conv2_3x3_int16` | GoogLeNet conv layer, INT16, data checked |
| `pdp_max_pooling_int16` | PDP max pooling with INT16 data verification |
| `sdp_relu_int16` | SDP ReLU with INT16 data verification |
| `cc_alexnet_conv5_relu5_int16_dtest_cvsram` | AlexNet conv5+relu5, INT16, CVSRAM |

## How to Build and Run Tests

```bash
# 1. Create tree.make
cat > tree.make << '"'"'EOF'"'"'
PROJECTS  := nv_full
OUTDIR    := outdir
CPP       := cpp
GCC       := g++
PERL      := perl
VERILATOR := verilator
CLANG     := clang
EOF

# 2. Create outdir symlink
mkdir -p outdir/nv_full
ln -sfn /app/vmod outdir/nv_full/vmod

# 3. Verilator elaboration (from verif/verilator/)
cd verif/verilator
mkdir -p /app/outdir/nv_full/verilator
verilator --cc --exe \
    -f verilator.f nvdla.cpp \
    --Mdir /app/outdir/nv_full/verilator \
    --output-split 5000000 --output-split-cfuncs 5000000

# 4. Compile
make -j8 -C /app/outdir/nv_full/verilator -f VNV_nvdla.mk CC=gcc CXX=g++

# 5. Run an E2E test
TEST=conv_8x8_fc_int16
mkdir -p /app/outdir/nv_full/verilator/test/${TEST}
perl input_txn_to_verilator.pl \
    /app/verif/traces/traceplayer/${TEST} \
    /app/outdir/nv_full/verilator/test/${TEST}/trace.bin

cd /app/outdir/nv_full/verilator/test/${TEST}
/app/outdir/nv_full/verilator/VNV_nvdla trace.bin
# Should print: *** PASS
```

## Module Organization

```
vmod/nvdla/
├── top/         NV_nvdla.v (full-chip instantiation)
├── bdma/        Bulk DMA
├── cacc/        Convolution accumulator
├── car/         Clock-and-reset
├── cbuf/        Convolution buffer (SRAM interface)
├── cdma/        Convolution DMA (fetches weights + feature maps)
├── cdp/         Channel data path (LRN)
├── cmac/        MAC array (core computation engine)
├── csb_master/  CSB register bus
├── csc/         Convolution sequence controller
├── glb/         Global controller / interrupt
├── nocif/       AXI4 interfaces (primary memory + CVSRAM)
├── pdp/         Planar data path (pooling)
├── retiming/    Optional pipeline registers
├── rubik/       Data reshape
└── sdp/         Single data path (batch norm, bias, activation, LUT)
```

The C-model in `cmod/` provides high-level reference behavior for each block —
use it to understand what each module must compute.

## Important: Partial Credit and Persistence

You are scored **proportionally** — each of the 7 E2E tests that passes earns
1/7 of the total reward. You do NOT need to complete the whole design.

**Do not give up or stop early because the task looks large.** The E2E tests
require the full pipeline, but you can still make progress by implementing
the most critical blocks first: `CDMA` (memory access), `CSC`/`CMAC`/`CACC`
(convolution core), `SDP` (post-processing), and `NOCIF` (AXI interface).
Even getting the convolution blocks right will enable multiple tests to pass.

You have up to 24 hours. Work incrementally — implement a block, check that
Verilator elaborates without errors, then run the simplest E2E trace. Use the
C-model in `cmod/` as a behavioral reference for each block'"'"'s logic.
